 "template": "In the Odoo Sales app, create a new quotation (Sales > Orders > Quotations, click New). In the Customer field, type '{{v1}}' and select the matching option from the autocomplete dropdown (it must actually be chosen from the dropdown, not just typed). Then add exactly ONE order line: in the product column of the first order line, click the product field and pick any product from the product catalogue via the autocomplete dropdown (it must actually be chosen from the dropdown). Set that line's quantity to 3. Do NOT add any second line yet. Read and report: (a) the exact product name you chose, (b) the unit price the app automatically filled in for that line, and (c) the Untaxed Amount the app computes at the bottom of the order. Do not confirm or save-as-anything other than leaving it as a draft quotation. Note: Odoo long-polls so never wait for network idle; wait for concrete page state instead.",
